! C22-6578 PROBLEM 1.4, "REPLACEMENT OF FULL WORDS BY ZEROS", printed
! p.7 (PDF 8), read in the ink.
!
!   "Replace the contents of full words DOG through DOG + 24.0 with
!   zeros."
!
! Three methods, each on its own 25 words with a guard word either
! side: the 25th word zeroed and the 26th not is the whole test.
!
! ONE CHANGE TO THE PRINTED TEXT, marked in place.  Each method ends in
! its own halt -- "B BEW, B" and "BEW, $" -- and a deck has one halt,
! so a printed halt that is not the last is replaced by a branch to the
! next method, with an SX of the index word in front of it so its
! final state can be read.
!
! THE INDEX WORD'S FINAL STATE IS THE PAGE'S OWN POINT.  Method 1
! comment (a): "The address field of the BEW instructions and the
! refill field of the index word are being used for identification
! purposes ... one can examine the refill field of $3 to find out the
! source of the index information."  Reference Manual printed p.26:
! CB+ adds ONE to the value in bit position 17, "increment, count and
! refill operations are independent of the success of the branch", and
! CB (no R) does not refill.  So after M1, $3 = 25.0, count 0, refill
! XW3.  After M2, $3 = DOG2 - 1.0 (the value stepped below the area),
! count 0, refill XW3A, flag and sign clear.
!
! Method 2's "CB-, $3, $-0.32" is itself part of the test: a half-word
! back from the CB- is the Z, and comment (a) spells out that a half
! word inserted between them would break it.

        SLC, 1000.0

! --- Method 1 ------------------------------------------------------
START   LX, $3, XW3
A       Z, DOG1($3)
        CB+, $3, A
B       SX, $3, FIN1
        B, M2
XW3     XW, 0.0, 25, XW3

! --- Method 2 ------------------------------------------------------
M2      LX, $3, XW3A
        Z, 0($3)
        CB-, $3, $-0.32
        SX, $3, FIN2
        B, M3
XW3A    XW, DOG2 + 24.0, 25, $

! --- Method 3 ------------------------------------------------------
M3      Z, DOG3
        TI, 12, DOG3, DOG3 + 1.0
        TI, 12, DOG3, DOG3 + 13.0
HALT    BEW, $

        SLC, 1100.0
FIN1    DD(BU,64,8), 0
FIN2    DD(BU,64,8), 0

! Three areas of sevens: a guard, the 25 words, a guard.
        SLC, 1110.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
DOG1    DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        SLC, 1200.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
DOG2    DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        SLC, 1300.0
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
DOG3    DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
        DD(BU,64,8), 7
